    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Top blocked source addresses",
      "description": "Extracted from the line at query time, never indexed — ADR-0003 keeps addresses out of the labels, and a label per source address is the textbook way to detonate Loki's cardinality. Anchored on the adjacent src,dst pair rather than a CSV field offset, because pfSense's IPv6 layout puts src at a different index; v6 lines therefore do not appear here. An empty table over a window with blocks in it means the regex stopped matching.",
      "datasource": {
